# Netlify _redirects — pretty URLs.
# https://docs.netlify.com/routing/redirects/
#
# Netlify's "Pretty URLs" feature is on by default for deploys, but we
# add explicit 200-rewrites for the canonical short paths the
# security.txt + Responsible Disclosure documents reference. Explicit
# rules guard against a future Netlify config change that flips Pretty
# URLs off.

/security        /security.html         200
/status          /status.html           200
/docs            /docs.html             200
/cctp-explainer  /cctp-explainer.html   200
/demo            /demo.html             200

# Treasury OpenAPI spec was pulled from the public surface 2026-05-12.
# It is operator-internal — no merchant use case, exposed internal
# architecture. Source of truth remains api/openapi/treasury.yaml in
# the monorepo for internal tooling. Anyone hitting the public path
# (cached bookmark, old marketing copy, scraper) gets a 410 Gone so
# they don't treat it as "temporarily missing".
#
# Netlify _redirects 410 syntax is `path  410` (no destination, no `!`).
# The previous `/api/treasury.yaml  410!` was malformed and Netlify
# silently fell back to a plain 404.
/api/treasury.yaml  410
